\"1710.05284v1\", \"title\": \"Multivariate Generalized Linear Mixed Models for Joint Estimation of Sporting Outcomes\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.05284v1\", \"published\": \"2017-10-15T06:40:00Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Report score 2: Ordinal logistic regression plus-minus player ratings, reviewed with GSE player-valuation work.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1706.04943v1\", \"title\": \"Plus-Minus Player Ratings for Soccer\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.04943v1\", \"published\": \"2017-06-15T16:01:58Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Soccer plus-minus ratings including xG plus-minus and expected-points plus-minus; APM variants transferable to player ratings.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1702.05982v1\", \"title\": \"Wages of wins: could an amateur make money from match outcome predictions?\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.05982v1\", \"published\": \"2017-02-17T12:12:57Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Report score 2: Elo-based player rating systems reviewed with GSE rating-method comparison.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1606.02825v2\", \"title\": \"Arbitrage-Free Combinatorial Market Making via Integer Programming\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.02825v2\", \"published\": \"2016-06-09T04:59:50Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Arbitrage-free combinatorial market making via integer programming with Frank-Wolfe Bregman projection, demonstrated on a 2^63-outcome NCAA bracket space; novel market-microstructure method for parlay/market pricing.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1603.05583v1\", \"title\": \"Analyzing In-Game Movements of Soccer Players at Scale\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05583v1\", \"published\": \"2016-03-11T23:54:55Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Large-scale soccer player movement profiles derived from event data without dedicated tracking systems, with player-similarity and replacement identification; novel physical-performance profiling for player evaluation.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1512.00894v1\", \"title\": \"Untangling Performance from Success\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.00894v1\", \"published\": \"2015-12-02T22:45:22Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Tennis performance-versus-popularity study; sociology of fame, not prediction.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1501.07179v1\", \"title\": \"Who's good this year? Comparing the Information Content of Games in the Four Major US Sports\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.07179v1\", \"published\": \"2015-01-28T16:31:47Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Information content per game quantified across the four major US sports via paired-comparison predictability curves; directly relevant sample-size guidance for ratings.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1312.4699v1\", \"title\": \"piBUSS: a parallel BEAST/BEAGLE utility for sequence simulation under complex evolutionary scenarios\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1312.4699v1\", \"published\": \"2013-12-17T09:43:17Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"piBUSS phylogenetic sequence simulation; bioinformatics, irrelevant.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1303.7177v2\", \"title\": \"High-frequency market-making for multi-dimensional Markov processes\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.7177v2\", \"published\": \"2013-03-28T16:59:04Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"High-frequency market-making for multi-dimensional Markov processes with HJB inventory control; could transfer to in-play odds-making microstructure.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1206.4810v1\", \"title\": \"High-frequency market-making with inventory constraints and directional bets\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1206.4810v1\", \"published\": \"2012-06-21T08:40:35Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"HFT market-making with inventory constraints and directional bets; tangential in-play pricing theory.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1108.1262v1\", \"title\": \"1st International Workshop on Complex Systems in Sports - Proceedings\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1108.1262v1\", \"published\": \"2011-08-05T07:30:45Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Complex-systems-in-sports workshop proceedings index; no methods content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1004.1292v1\", \"title\": \"A Stochastic Analysis of some Two-Person Sports\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1004.1292v1\", \"published\": \"2010-04-08T09:33:04Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Rally-level stochastic analysis of side-out versus rally-point scoring in two-person sports; transferable to set/game probability modeling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"0803.3697v1\", \"title\": \"In-season prediction of batting averages: A field test of empirical Bayes and Bayes methodologies\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/0803.3697v1\", \"published\": \"2008-03-26T11:00:46Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": null, \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Empirical Bayes in-season batting-average prediction validated on held-out months; classic shrinkage estimation directly relevant to player-ability estimation.\"}\n"}
{"id": "arxiv-sweep/scored_batch_3.jsonl", "corpus": "arxiv-sweep", "kind": "scored", "chars": 54729, "equations": ["e^\\\\pm"], "text": "{\"id\": \"2609.16538v1\", \"title\": \"Learning Transferable Self-Supervised Priors for Super-Resolution Reconstruction in Structured Illumination Microscopy\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.16538v1\", \"published\": \"2026-09-15T02:34:13Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"point_spread\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Super-resolution microscopy method with no transfer to sports prediction.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2609.12651v1\", \"title\": \"Distortion of AI Alignment Revisited: RLHF is a Decent Utilitarian Aligner\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.12651v1\", \"published\": \"2026-09-11T09:55:06Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Bradley-Terry theory applied to RLHF distortion; tangential to rating-link theory.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2609.08082v2\", \"title\": \"Inference-Time Nash Alignment\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08082v2\", \"published\": \"2026-09-08T00:50:12Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Nash equilibrium over general preferences via Best-of-Nash; tangential game-theoretic preference theory.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2609.06739v1\", \"title\": \"The profit-bias identity in sports betting: bookmaker profit as the public's prediction error\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.06739v1\", \"published\": \"2026-09-06T17:22:25Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"baseball_sabermetrics\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Gives GSE a clean accounting framework for *where* book margin comes from \\u2014 directly tells you which leg (hold vs.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2609.01337v1\", \"title\": \"LEAP: Likelihood Elicitation and Aggregation for LLM-based Probabilistic Forecasting\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.01337v1\", \"published\": \"2026-09-01T14:49:19Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"calibration_sports\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"This is a concrete, implementable anti-monolith pattern: separate evidence\\u2192likelihood from prior\\u2192posterior combination.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2608.25350v1\", \"title\": \"Beyond Pairwise Feedback: Listwise Vision-Language Supervision for Preference-Based Reward Learning\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.25350v1\", \"published\": \"2026-08-26T04:09:21Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Listwise Plackett-Luce ranking for VLM reward learning; formulation could transfer to rank aggregation.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2608.16710v1\", \"title\": \"The Ethical Decision Head: Operationalizing Normative Ethics in Autonomous Vehicles via Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.16710v1\", \"published\": \"2026-08-17T15:26:09Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Ethical RL for autonomous vehicles; no sports prediction content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2608.10567v1\", \"title\": \"DashArena: Benchmarking LLMs on Interactive Analytic Dashboard Generation\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.10567v1\", \"published\": \"2026-08-11T06:54:37Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Benchmark for generating analytic dashboards; tangential to GSE's analytics tooling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2608.08491v1\", \"title\": \"TrustRoboReward: Preference-Ordered Isotonic Score Editing for Multi-Paradigm Robot Reward Models\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.08491v1\", \"published\": \"2026-08-09T05:25:22Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Robotic manipulation reward modeling; no sports application.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2608.05030v1\", \"title\": \"From Score Matrices to Football-Aware Match-State Simulation: An Auditable LLM Harness for Exact-Score Reranking\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.05030v1\", \"published\": \"2026-08-05T16:34:53Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"expected_goals; poisson_simple\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"The *architecture* is the value: statistical core (Dixon\\u2013Coles) + LLM restricted to contextual parameter adjustments + goal-by-goal simulation over a candidate set, with explicit negative findings about where football-aware simulation does NOT help (tail candidates added coverage, zero Top-3 hits).\"}\n{\"id\": \"2608.02081v1\", \"title\": \"Isotonic Bradley-Terry Model for Paired Comparison Data\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.02081v1\", \"published\": \"2026-08-03T11:37:56Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry; baseball_sabermetrics\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Every rating system GSE runs assumes logistic (or probit) link.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2607.22221v1\", \"title\": \"Convergence analysis of a family of Zermelo-type iterations for the Bradley--Terry model\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.22221v1\", \"published\": \"2026-07-24T11:39:24Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Faster Zermelo-type fixed-point iterations for Bradley-Terry MLE; directly speeds GSE's rating computation.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2607.15766v1\", \"title\": \"Before the Action: Benchmarking LLMs on Prospective Hypothesis Discovery\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.15766v1\", \"published\": \"2026-07-17T08:56:43Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"LLM hypothesis-discovery benchmark; tangential to automated research discovery.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2607.14180v1\", \"title\": \"RENEW: Towards Learning World Models and Repairing Model Exploitation from Preferences\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.14180v1\", \"published\": \"2026-07-15T14:03:45Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Preference-based repair of world-model exploitation; tangential to sports world models.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2607.07320v1\", \"title\": \"SoccerNet 2026 Challenges Results\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.07320v1\", \"published\": \"2026-07-08T12:06:48Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"calibration_sports\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Public, current, competition-scale benchmark for exactly the video\\u2192tracking\\u2192anticipation pipeline GSE wants for NGS benchmarking.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2607.01722v2\", \"title\": \"An Adaptive Glicko-2 Rating Framework for Probabilistic Football Forecasting and Season Simulation\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.01722v2\", \"published\": \"2026-07-02T05:21:38Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"glicko\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"A checklist of Glicko-2 extensions with explicit uncertainty modeling (Glicko-2 carries rating deviation, which plain Elo lacks).\"}\n{\"id\": \"2606.24391v1\", \"title\": \"Age of LLM: A Strategic 1v1 Benchmark for Reasoning, Diplomacy and Reliability of Large Language Models under Fog of War\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.24391v1\", \"published\": \"2026-06-23T10:25:31Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"LLM game benchmark under fog of war; no sports prediction content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2606.21146v1\", \"title\": \"ChronoLock: Protecting Videos from Unauthorized Text-to-Video Personalization\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.21146v1\", \"published\": \"2026-06-19T06:37:13Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"transformer_simple\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Video protection against T2V personalization; no prediction content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2606.17056v1\", \"title\": \"The Value Axis: Language Models Encode Whether They're on the Right Track\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.17056v1\", \"published\": \"2026-06-15T17:59:58Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"expected_goals\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Internal 'value axis' in LLMs; no sports application.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2606.13221v2\", \"title\": \"From Uncertain Judgments to Calibrated Rankings: Conformal Elo Estimation for LLM Evaluation\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.13221v2\", \"published\": \"2026-06-11T11:38:05Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Two immediately stealable ideas: (1) *feed calibrated probabilities, not hard 0/1 outcomes, into your rating updates* \\u2014 for GSE this means updating ratings from model-implied win probabilities with uncertainty, not just realized outcomes; (2) split conformal intervals on rating residuals give **distribution-free coverage** \\u2014 a mathematically clean upgrade over quantile-regression calibration that makes no distributional assumptions.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2606.09327v1\", \"title\": \"A Universal Dense Football Event Representation Based on TabTransformer\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.09327v1\", \"published\": \"2026-06-08T10:47:47Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"calibration_sports; transformer_simple\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"This is the embedding layer GSE's play-by-play pipeline lacks: pretrained dense representations of events with *better calibration as a measured outcome*.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2606.04387v1\", \"title\": \"Rethinking Sales Lead Scoring with LLM-based Hierarchical Preference Ranking\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.04387v1\", \"published\": \"2026-06-03T03:05:57Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"LLM hierarchical preference ranking for sales leads; ranking formulation could transfer.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2606.01504v1\", \"title\": \"Semantic Retrieval for Product Search in E-Commerce\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.01504v1\", \"published\": \"2026-05-31T23:59:32Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"E-commerce semantic retrieval; no sports content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2605.30552v1\", \"title\": \"High-Fidelity 3D Simulator for Synthetic fNIRS Data Generation\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.30552v1\", \"published\": \"2026-05-28T20:34:27Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"monte_carlo_sports\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"fNIRS brain-imaging simulator; no prediction content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2607.26061v1\", \"title\": \"Sim2Win: A Team-Agnostic, Event-Based Pre-Match Outcome Prediction and Tactical Profiling System for Football\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.26061v1\", \"published\": \"2026-05-26T01:46:46Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"football_prediction\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Proves behavioral/tactical representations transfer across distributions where identity-based ratings can't (new teams, new leagues \\u2014 think CFB with roster churn).\"}\n{\"id\": \"2605.23854v1\", \"title\": \"Entrywise Error Bounds for Spectral Ranking with Semi-Random Adversaries\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.23854v1\", \"published\": \"2026-05-22T17:08:07Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"bradley_terry\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Entrywise error bounds for spectral BTL ranking under adversarial graphs; directly relevant to rating robustness.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2605.14855v1\", \"title\": \"Exploitation of Hidden Context in Dynamic Movement Forecasting: A Neural Network Journey from Recurrent to Graph Neural Networks and General Purpose Transformers\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.14855v1\", \"published\": \"2026-05-14T14:02:45Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"gnn_sports; transformer_simple\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"A like-for-like empirical comparison of exactly the trajectory-forecasting stack relevant to NGS-style tracking metrics (NGS's expected-rush/receiving models are trajectory-adjacent).\"}\n{\"id\": \"2605.04724v2\", \"title\": \"From Beats to Breaches:How Offensive AI Infers Sensitive User Information from Playlists\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.04724v2\", \"published\": \"2026-05-06T10:18:55Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"gnn_sports\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"PII inference from music playlists; no sports content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2604.27865v1\", \"title\": \"KellyBench: A Benchmark for Long-Horizon Sequential Decision Making\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.27865v1\", \"published\": \"2026-04-30T13:47:22Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"sports_betting_ml; odds_modeling\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Public, API-accessible **bankroll-growth benchmark** for betting strategies \\u2014 GSE can run its own staking/edge logic through KellyBench-style sequential evaluation instead of backtesting single bets.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2604.09143v1\", \"title\": \"Score-Driven Rating System for Sports\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.09143v1\", \"published\": \"2026-04-10T09:22:33Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"elo_rating\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"This is the *theory GSE's rating updates are missing*: it shows Elo-style updates are a special case of score-driven (GAS) updates, so any likelihood you can write down (margin of victory, EPA distributions, rankings) induces a principled rating update with proven consistency/fairness properties.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2603.25901v1\", \"title\": \"Decoding Defensive Coverage Responsibilities in American Football Using Factorized Attention Based Transformer Models\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.25901v1\", \"published\": \"2026-03-26T20:43:30Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"nfl_model\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"NFL-authored (includes Keegan Abdoo / Mike Band of NFL NGS-adjacent work), 89%+ on a genuinely hard task, and the *factorized attention* design plus *truncated-trajectory training* are directly reusable patterns for any GSE tracking-data model.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2603.17866v3\", \"title\": \"NFL step-and-turn: A generative framework for evaluating player movement in American football\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.17866v3\", \"published\": \"2026-03-18T15:54:28Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"player_tracking\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"The \\\"evaluate against the distribution of what *could* have happened\\\" framing is the principled version of rush-yards-over-expected \\u2014 instead of comparing to an average outcome, you compare to a *personalized posterior predictive distribution* of the same player's movement.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2603.06863v1\", \"title\": \"A prior information informed learning architecture for flying trajectory prediction\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.06863v1\", \"published\": \"2026-03-06T20:33:07Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"transformer_simple\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Tennis-ball landing-point prediction with dual-transformer; directly relevant to trajectory-based prop modeling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2602.23288v1\", \"title\": \"BRIDGE: Borderless Reconfiguration for Inclusive and Diverse Gameplay Experience via Embodiment Transformation\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.23288v1\", \"published\": \"2026-02-26T18:01:35Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"transformer_simple\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Broadcast-video player reconstruction for parasports; tangential to tracking pipeline.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2602.18981v1\", \"title\": \"How Far Can We Go with Pixels Alone? A Pilot Study on Screen-Only Navigation in Commercial 3D ARPGs\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.18981v1\", \"published\": \"2026-02-21T23:15:18Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"expected_goals\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Screen-only navigation in ARPGs; no sports content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2602.15181v1\", \"title\": \"Time-Archival Camera Virtualization for Sports and Visual Performances\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.15181v1\", \"published\": \"2026-02-16T20:39:51Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"transformer_simple\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Novel-view synthesis for sports broadcasts; tangential broadcast tech, no predictive method.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2602.02321v1\", \"title\": \"Surface Interactions in Photon Monte Carlo Simulations\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.02321v1\", \"published\": \"2026-02-02T16:49:23Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"point_spread\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Photon Monte 