formal methods beat parametric calibration on sports win probabilities.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2206.07212v2\", \"title\": \"Explainable expected goal models for performance analysis in football analytics\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.07212v2\", \"published\": \"2022-06-14T23:56:03Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"expected_goals\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Explainable xG models for football analytics; directly relevant to prop and match modeling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2205.02977v1\", \"title\": \"IMU Based Deep Stride Length Estimation With Self-Supervised Learning\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.02977v1\", \"published\": \"2022-05-06T01:48:39Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"calibration_sports\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"IMU stride-length estimation; no prediction content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2204.04049v1\", \"title\": \"Efficient tracking of team sport players with few game-specific annotations\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.04049v1\", \"published\": \"2022-04-08T13:11:30Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"player_tracking\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Full-game team-sport player tracking with few annotations; directly relevant to tracking pipeline.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2203.02281v2\", \"title\": \"A Comprehensive Review of Computer Vision in Sports: Open Issues, Future Trends and Research Directions\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.02281v2\", \"published\": \"2022-03-03T07:49:21Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"player_tracking\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Comprehensive review of computer vision in sports; tangential overview.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2201.04480v2\", \"title\": \"Learning to Identify Top Elo Ratings: A Dueling Bandits Approach\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.04480v2\", \"published\": \"2022-01-12T13:57:29Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"elo_rating\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Dueling-bandit online match scheduling for sample-efficient Elo estimation; directly relevant to ratings and bandits.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2110.14632v1\", \"title\": \"Heterogeneous Effects of Software Patches in a Multiplayer Online Battle Arena Game\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.14632v1\", \"published\": \"2021-10-27T17:59:22Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"causal_sports\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Causal inference on patch effects in LoL; tangential method transfer.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2109.15046v2\", \"title\": \"An Elo-type rating model for players and teams of variable strength\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.15046v2\", \"published\": \"2021-09-28T12:30:26Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"elo_rating\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Kinetic Elo-type rating model for variable strength; directly relevant to rating theory.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2108.02419v1\", \"title\": \"Implementing the BBE Agent-Based Model of a Sports-Betting Exchange\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.02419v1\", \"published\": \"2021-08-05T07:29:24Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"sports_betting_ml\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"A public **exchange simulator** \\u2014 GSE can test staking, market-making, and in-play strategies against synthetic order flow instead of risking real bankroll.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2107.06495v4\", \"title\": \"ggViz: Accelerating Large-Scale Esports Game Analysis\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2107.06495v4\", \"published\": \"2021-07-14T05:48:26Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"player_tracking; win_probability\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Sketch-based esports game-state querying with WP charts; tangential analytics concept.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2106.05174v1\", \"title\": \"UEFA EURO 2020 Forecast via Nested Zero-Inflated Generalized Poisson Regression\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.05174v1\", \"published\": \"2021-06-09T16:17:24Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"poisson_simple\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Nested zero-inflated generalized Poisson + Elo covariates for EURO 2020 forecasting; directly relevant to score modeling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2105.13472v2\", \"title\": \"How a Losing Team like the Canadiens can Steal a Stanley Cup: A Quantitative Intransitive Hockey Analysis\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2105.13472v2\", \"published\": \"2021-05-26T03:18:11Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"hockey_prediction\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Intransitive matchup theory under salary caps in hockey; tangential transfer to matchup modeling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2104.14012v1\", \"title\": \"Simplified Kalman filter for online rating: one-fits-all approach\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.14012v1\", \"published\": \"2021-04-28T20:44:10Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"glicko\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Unifies GSE's rating zoo into one Kalman-filtering framework \\u2014 one implementation, any likelihood, with uncertainty propagation built in.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2104.03252v2\", \"title\": \"Leaving Goals on the Pitch: Evaluating Decision Making in Soccer\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.03252v2\", \"published\": \"2021-04-07T16:56:31Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"expected_goals\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"A reusable pattern \\u2014 learn the behavioral MDP, then counterfactual-query it \\u2014 applicable to NFL play-calling (run/pass, fourth-down, red-zone decisions).\"}\n{\"id\": \"2012.04378v2\", \"title\": \"Forecasting the Olympic medal distribution during a pandemic: a socio-economic machine learning model\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.04378v2\", \"published\": \"2020-12-08T11:50:14Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"sports_betting_ml; odds_modeling\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Two-stage random forest for Olympic medal forecasting; directly relevant to performance prediction.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2010.12508v1\", \"title\": \"Beating the market with a bad predictive model\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.12508v1\", \"published\": \"2020-10-23T16:20:35Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"sports_betting_ml; kelly_criterion\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"This inverts GSE's training paradigm: stop minimizing prediction error vs.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2008.04216v3\", \"title\": \"Using Experts' Opinions in Machine Learning Tasks\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.04216v3\", \"published\": \"2020-08-10T15:48:49Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"odds_modeling; betting_odds_pred\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"A principled recipe for what GSE already does informally \\u2014 blend market odds and expert signal into the model.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2006.04551v4\", \"title\": \"Cracking the Black Box: Distilling Deep Sports Analytics\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.04551v4\", \"published\": \"2020-06-04T01:49:36Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"deep_learning_analytics\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Distilling deep sports models into interpretable linear model trees; directly relevant to GSE's interpretability lane.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2003.13962v1\", \"title\": \"Multi-Modal Graph Neural Network for Joint Reasoning on Vision and Scene Text\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.13962v1\", \"published\": \"2020-03-31T05:56:59Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"gnn_sports\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Multi-modal GNN for visual question answering; no sports content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2002.04148v1\", \"title\": \"The role of intrinsic dimension in high-resolution player tracking data -- Insights in basketball\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.04148v1\", \"published\": \"2020-02-11T00:34:32Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"player_tracking\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Intrinsic dimension is a genuinely novel descriptor for tracking data \\u2014 a single number capturing play complexity/predictability.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1910.12337v1\", \"title\": \"Expected Hypothetical Completion Probability\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.12337v1\", \"published\": \"2019-10-27T20:07:26Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"player_tracking\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"This is the methodological ancestor of NGS's completion-probability family, with the imputation trick s