arisons Using Player Tracking Data\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.04351v2\", \"published\": \"2015-11-13T16:40:28Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"player_tracking\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"PCA dimensionality reduction of NBA tracking data for player comparison; directly relevant to tracking analytics.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1412.0248v1\", \"title\": \"Building an NCAA mens basketball predictive model and quantifying its success\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1412.0248v1\", \"published\": \"2014-11-30T17:09:17Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"basketball_prediction\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"NCAA basketball prediction model and tournament-pool luck quantification; directly relevant to contest theory.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1310.6998v1\", \"title\": \"Predicting the NFL using Twitter\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.6998v1\", \"published\": \"2013-10-25T18:35:22Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"sports_betting_ml; nfl_model\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"NFL win/spread/total prediction using Twitter features; directly relevant to text-as-features and NFL modeling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1302.4175v1\", \"title\": \"A High Rate Tension Device for Characterizing Brain Tissue\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1302.4175v1\", \"published\": \"2013-02-18T07:57:46Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"calibration_sports\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Brain tissue tension device; no sports content.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1205.4750v1\", \"title\": \"First Order Approximations of the Pythagorean Won-Loss Formula for Predicting MLB Teams' Winning Percentages\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1205.4750v1\", \"published\": \"2012-05-21T21:04:36Z\", \"wave\": null, \"query\": \"baseball_sabermetrics\", \"score\": 2, \"rationale\": \"Pythagorean formula as first-order linear approximation for MLB win%; directly relevant to win-pct modeling theory.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1107.0302v1\", \"title\": \"Reproducing entanglement through local classical resources with no communication\", \"