{"id": "arxiv-sweep/scored_batch_5.jsonl", "corpus": "arxiv-sweep", "kind": "scored", "chars": 117543, "equations": ["L^p"], "text": "{\"id\": \"2601.12896v3\", \"title\": \"Quantitative Methods in Finance\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.12896v3\", \"published\": \"2026-01-19T09:50:52Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Graduate lecture notes unifying probability, statistics, and Monte Carlo methods for finance; useful background toolkit but not sports-specific.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2505.11566v1\", \"title\": \"Theory: Multidimensional Space of Events\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.11566v1\", \"published\": \"2025-05-16T08:54:12Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Proposes a multidimensional event-space extension of Bayesian probability for mutual influences; theoretical and tangential to sports prediction.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2501.08710v2\", \"title\": \"Disentangled Interleaving Variational Encoding\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.08710v2\", \"published\": \"2025-01-15T10:50:54Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Designs a marginal/conditional-probability-inspired disentangling method for multi-task learning; transferable representation idea but not sports.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2409.12783v1\", \"title\": \"Financial Stochastic Models Diffusion: From Risk-Neutral to Real-World Measure\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.12783v1\", \"published\": \"2024-09-19T13:51:14Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Builds a Girsanov-theorem framework for moving financial diffusions from risk-neutral to real-world measure; finance-domain, only conceptually transferable to odds modeling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2408.06797v1\", \"title\": \"Stunned by Sleeping Beauty: How Prince Probability updates his forecast upon their fateful encounter\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.06797v1\", \"published\": \"2024-08-13T10:27:16Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Analyzes the Sleeping Beauty probability puzzle; philosophy of probability with no transferable method.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2303.11536v2\", \"title\": \"Indeterminate Probability Theory\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.11536v2\", \"published\": \"2023-03-21T01:57:40Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Proposes Indeterminate Probability Theory, an observer-centered framework combining ground truth with observation error; theoretical, weak transfer to measurement-error modeling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2209.02292v1\", \"title\": \"Emergence of universal scaling in weather extreme events\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.02292v1\", \"published\": \"2022-09-06T08:40:46Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Finds universal scaling in weather-extreme statistics via statistical physics; climate domain, no sports transfer.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2204.13087v2\", \"title\": \"Faster online calibration without randomization: interval forecasts and the power of two choices\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.13087v2\", \"published\": \"2022-04-27T17:33:23Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Proves tight O(1/sqrt(T)) calibration bounds and gives a faster deterministic online calibration method via power-of-two-choices interval forecasts; directly applicable to calibrating GSE probabilistic forecasts.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2108.03210v3\", \"title\": \"Regression Diagnostics meets Forecast Evaluation: Conditional Calibration, Reliability Diagrams, and Coefficient of Determination\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.03210v3\", \"published\": \"2021-08-06T17:21:48Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Develops a general theory of calibration for distributional regression with conditional calibration, reliability diagrams, and R^2 analogues; core new math for validating GSE forecast reliability.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2108.02140v1\", \"title\": \"Linear regression under model uncertainty\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.02140v1\", \"published\": \"2021-08-04T16:12:55Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Reexamines linear regression under mean/variance uncertainty via sublinear expectation; theoretical robust-regression work, tangential.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2012.04455v1\", \"title\": \"Ratio of counts vs ratio of rates in Poisson processes\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.04455v1\", \"published\": \"2020-12-07T16:23:02Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Distinguishes predictive vs inferential ratio problems for counts vs rates in Poisson processes; mildly useful for Poisson goal/point modeling but basic.\"}\n{\"id\": \"0901.1945v1\", \"title\": \"A mathematical proof of the existence of trends in financial time series\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.1945v1\", \"published\": \"2009-01-14T07:47:18Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prob_theory_pred\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Claims a nonstandard-analysis proof of trends in financial time series; finance philosophy, no transferable method.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2512.14727v1\", \"title\": \"A Critical Perspective on Finite Sample Conformal Prediction Theory in Medical Applications\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.14727v1\", \"published\": \"2025-12-09T16:59:31Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Critiques finite-sample conformal prediction guarantees in medical applications; the conformal-prediction angle transfers to prediction intervals but the focus is medical.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2512.00342v2\", \"title\": \"Adaptive prediction theory combining offline and online learning\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.00342v2\", \"published\": \"2025-11-29T06:13:47Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Initiates theory for two-stage offline-plus-online prediction on nonlinear stochastic dynamical systems; directly relevant to adapting GSE models online to non-stationary sports data.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2505.04198v2\", \"title\": \"A Predictive Theory of Electrochemical Ostwald Ripening for Electrodeposited Lithium Metal\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.04198v2\", \"published\": \"2025-05-07T07:53:01Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Models electrochemical Ostwald ripening in lithium-metal anodes; battery chemistry, irrelevant.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2402.04143v5\", \"title\": \"Quantitative Predictive Theories through Integrating Quantum, Statistical, Equilibrium, and Nonequilibrium Thermodynamics\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.04143v5\", \"published\": \"2024-02-06T16:49:23Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Integrates quantum, statistical, equilibrium, and nonequilibrium thermodynamics; physics, irrelevant.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2111.08560v1\", \"title\": \"Prediction theory in continuous time\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2111.08560v1\", \"published\": \"2021-11-16T15:38:31Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Gives short proofs of classical continuous-time prediction theory for stationary processes; textbook-level, weak transfer.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2108.07728v1\", \"title\": \"Predictive Theory of Neutrino Masses\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.07728v1\", \"published\": \"2021-08-13T12:38:30Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Predicts neutrino masses from quantum-gravity couplings; particle physics, irrelevant.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2106.03589v3\", \"title\": \"Nonparametric adaptive control and prediction: theory and randomized algorithms\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.03589v3\", \"published\": \"2021-06-07T13:15:40Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Introduces a nonparametric RKHS algorithm that learns an infinite-dimensional parameter density online for adaptive control; transferable online-learning theory but control-focused.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2104.13132v1\", \"title\": \"Stability of trigonometric approximation in $L^p$ and applications to prediction theory\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13132v1\", \"published\": \"2021-04-27T12:22:57Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Studies stability of trigonometric approximation in L^p with prediction-theory applications; pure math, irrelevant.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2104.12134v1\", \"title\": \"Advancing from phenomenological to predictive theory of ferroelectric oxide solution properties through consideration of domain walls\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.12134v1\", \"published\": \"2021-04-25T11:20:51Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Builds a predictive theory of ferroelectric oxide solution properties; materials science, irrelevant.\"}\n{\"id\": \"2011.09937v2\", \"title\": \"Prediction Theory for Stationary Functional Time Series\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.09937v2\", \"published\": \"2020-11-19T16:20:09Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Surveys prediction theory for stationary functional time series; high-level survey, weakly transferable to trajectory modeling.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1710.02950v2\", \"title\": \"Maximum Regularized Likelihood Estimators: A General Prediction Theory and Applications\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.02950v2\", \"published\": \"2017-10-09T06:16:50Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Derives KL-divergence guarantees for maximum regularized likelihood estimators across tensor regression and graphical models; general theory, tangential.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1703.02403v4\", \"title\": \"On Structured Prediction Theory with Calibrated Convex Surrogate Losses\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.02403v4\", \"published\": \"2017-03-07T14:39:15Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Constructs calibrated convex surrogates for structured prediction with tight calibration-function bounds; structured-prediction theory, weak transfer.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1702.07460v2\", \"title\": \"Tuning transcriptional regulation through signaling: A predictive theory of allosteric induction\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.07460v2\", \"published\": \"2017-02-24T04:12:20Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Models allosteric transcriptional regulation via the Monod-Wyman-Changeux model; biology, irrelevant.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1609.08773v1\", \"title\": \"Beyond the effective mass approximation: predictive theory of the nonlinear optical response of conduction electrons\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.08773v1\", \"published\": \"2016-09-28T05:09:30Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Studies nonlinear optical response of conduction electrons to THz fields; physics, irrelevant.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1605.06443v2\", \"title\": \"Structured Prediction Theory Based on Factor Graph Complexity\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.06443v2\", \"published\": \"2016-05-20T17:21:17Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Proves the tightest known data-dependent margin bounds for structured prediction via factor-graph complexity; theory, tangential.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1411.6243v2\", \"title\": \"Structure Regularization for Structured Prediction: Theories and Experiments\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.6243v2\", \"published\": \"2014-11-23T14:11:01Z\", \"wave\": 3, \"query\": \"prediction_theory\", \"score\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Argues complex