{"id": "arxiv-sweep/waves/wave7-worker3-status.jsonl", "corpus": "arxiv-sweep", "kind": "wave", "chars": 3945, "equations": [], "text": "{\"id\": \"2011.02122v1\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"ADAPT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0509-analysing-long-short-term-memory-models.md\", \"notes\": \"Cricket ball-by-ball LSTM (82.6% accuracy, log-loss 0.40, 0.5%/over improvement); adapt in-play spread/total surface LSTM for NFL live betting. Full text read (all pages).\"}\n{\"id\": \"2005.12661v2\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"ADAPT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0510-dagnet-double-attentive-graph-neural-network.md\", \"notes\": \"DAG-Net VRNN + dual attentive GNN for trajectory forecasting (basketball); adapt goal-conditioned graph trajectory modeling to NFL tracking (ball-carrier path, defender closeout). Full text read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1906.01760v3\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"ADOPT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0511-going-deep-models-for-continuoustime-withinplay.md\", \"notes\": \"Yurko et al. continuous-time within-play valuation with tracking data (multinomial logistic + random forest, 2017 NFL); foundational reference for GSE tracking lane. Full text read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1811.02885v1\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"REJECT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0512-player-availability-rating-par-a-tool.md\", \"notes\": \"Ad hoc NHL trade-availability formula; linear models underperform NHL.com/TSN baselines; no transfer path to GSE. Full text read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1804.03247v1\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"REJECT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0513-finegrained-activity-recognition-in-baseball-videos.md\", \"notes\": \"Baseball broadcast-video activity recognition (Faster R-CNN + 3D CNN); no GSE transfer path. Full text read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1802.08765v1\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"ADAPT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0514-model-trees-for-identifying-exceptional-players.md\", \"notes\": \"Logistic model trees for NHL draft zero-inflation (AUC ~0.75); adapt to NFL draft prospect modeling with interpretable explanations. Full text read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1710.06551v2\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"ADAPT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0515-exploiting-oddsmaker-bias-to-improve-the.md\", \"notes\": \"Shannon-entropy bet-selection on ATS spreads; TI Min-Entropy 71.85% but TD evidence tiny (12/18 at k=3), threshold set visually; re-test on multi-season closing lines before use. Full text read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1606.02011v3\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"ADAPT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0516-approximate-nonparametric-maximum-likelihood-inference-for.md\", \"notes\": \"Grid-based approximate NPMLE via convex optimization; bivariate (mean,noise) EB shrinkage beats univariate/James-Stein (baseball TSE 0.29 vs 0.54); adapt as GSE player/team shrinkage layer. Full text read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1505.06918v1\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"REJECT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0517-fantasy-football-prediction.md\", \"notes\": \"2015 QB fantasy SVR/NN study; best MAE 6.2 points (author admits unusable), no baselines, QB-only, 2009-2014 data; strictly weaker than GSE projections. Full text read.\"}\n{\"id\": \"1412.0248v1\", \"status\": \"completed\", \"verdict\": \"ADAPT\", \"ledger_path\": \"/home/hatch/workspace/vendor/Sports/docs/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0518-building-an-ncaa-mens-basketball-predictive.md\", \"notes\": \"Kaggle 2014 March Mania winner: spread-calibrated logistic + efficiency-model ensemble (weights tuned on past tournaments, 0.69/0.31); luck simulation shows even perfect probabilities win ~12% of 433-entry contests. Full text read.\"}\n"}
