n) blitzed 48.4% W1 vs 26.3% in 2025; MIN's 80.4% blitz was solved in-game by GB (83% 1H→63% 2H); LAC (O'Leary) 2025 results inflated by +7.11 INT luck (2nd-most); SF (Morris) 2026 five-man fronts, not four-down quarters.\n- Mechanical full-pool score = mean pool percentile − salary percentile (101 WR/TE): top values Caleb Douglas $3,700, Gesicki $3,600, Roman Wilson $3,200, M. Washington $4,000, K. Raymond $3,600; top traps R. Rice $6,400, Waddle $6,500, Ja'Marr Chase $7,600, Godwin $5,600 (69th/72 separation, 1.33 YPRR), McLaurin $5,200.\n- Weather: MIN@CHI 13 mph winds gusts 23–30, rain ~1 inch (3/5 impact); PIT@NE 2nd-half rain; CLE@TB 40% PM thunderstorm.\n## Data sources named\n- StatRankings CSV dump 2026-09-18 (players, teams, coverage, red-zone files), FantasyPoints bellcow, MediJo20 rushing scatter, sfdata9ers, magicsportsguy (CB assignments, receiver alignment, NYG-LAR context), FantasyPros, Sharp xFP, RotoWire audit, DK Network/Huddle [2P] salaries, CoverageIQ, NBC (Walker RYOE), PFF (WR ranks, LB grades, CB ratings: Johnson 113.7/44.8, Stevenson 158.3, Quentin Lake 0.17 FP/route 8th / 18.9% target rate allowed 3rd), SumerSports (JSN 45.8%, Lawrence +1.35 no-PA), Razzball zone/gap splits, eight [WEB] lanes 2026-09-19 ~11:05–11:45 CDT.\n## Findings (numbers and facts, not vibes)\n- 18 numbered corrections to prior research (team-affiliation errors: Likely→NYG Giant signed 3yr/$40M, Cousins→Raiders QB, Brissett→ARI, Rush→ATL starter, Pittman→PIT, Kirk→SF, Deebo→SF; Nabers faces LAR zone (85.3%) not McDuffie; Darnold out/Lock starts SEA; Purdy out/Jones starts; Myles Garrett traded to LAR, IR 9/17; Donald reduced situational snaps).\n- Injury resolutions: Mason IR 9/16 (thumb, out 4+ games); Bowers doubtful → Mayer 6/7 W1 pivot; Z. Flowers doubtful; Nico Collins OUT (Grade 1 hamstring) → Schultz ELITE ($3.2K vs CIN's 34.4-graded LBs); J. Jacobs on Commissioner's Exempt List 9/19; Adebo IR (NYG); Porter Jr. out.\n- Garrett's liked-play verdicts: Jefferson PLAY (role maximal, CHI 60% man soft); Bijan PLAY (45.5% share, CAR 124.9 zone yards); Javonte PLAY (95% XFP at $6,400 RB8); Mayer PLAY ($3,600, LAC 27th DVOA vs TEs, 77% TE catch rate); Henry PLAY (38.3 FPPG, 85.7% inside-5); Andrews PLAY (condensed pie, no Likely hedge exists); Schultz ELITE; Pitts FADE; Addison/Bateman CONDITIONAL on TPRR flags.\n- Best schematic offense boosts: TB vs CLE (+0.400 EPA/play allowed, 61.2% success, 22.4% explosive, 1.48 slot FP/rr); WAS vs DAL (+0.397, new DC Parker Fangio install); NYG vs LAR (+0.262; NYG +0.397 EPA/play, +0.677/db W1); CHI vs MIN (MIN 33.3% explosive allowed when blitz misses).\n- DST boosts: JAX vs DEN (four cuts deep: -0.493 allowed, 53.1% pressure, Nix QB31, takeaway-regression caveat +5.04 INT over expected 2025); KC vs IND; TB vs CLE (Watson benching risk, Monken -0.30); PHI vs TEN; NE vs PIT (48.1% blitz).\n- Backfield news: Kamara debut behind Etienne (caps Etienne); Henderson threatening Rhamondre's 85% share; Walker KC bellcow (23-to-8 over E. Johnson).\n## Intelligence connections (tag each: QB-BEHAVIOR, COACHING, OL, TRUST-SIGNAL, SCHEME, OTHER)\n- Target share / first-read share / TPRR / air-yard share concentration metrics (Jefferson 52.9% first-read, JSN 45.8% share, Puka 50% first-read, Pitts 5% TPRR): QB-BEHAVIOR (trust-target profiling — first-read share and TPRR identify whom the QB actually trusts).\n- Red-zone/goal-line rush-share monopolies (Taylor 100% inside-10/inside-5, Henry 85.7% inside-5, Javonte 100% inside-10) and RZ receiving TDs: QB-BEHAVIOR (red-zone tendencies — run vs pass, which back gets the call).\n- Zone/gap rush-scheme vs defense-yards-allowed mismatches (Bijan 57% zone vs CAR 124.9, CMC 90% vs MIA 65.2, Taylor tempered into KC 23.2): SCHEME, OL (scheme fit + implied run-blocking matchup quality).\n- Defensive man/zone/blitz rates + DC corrections (PIT 96.2% zone vs brand, GB 48.4% blitz spike, MIN blitz solved in-game): COACHING, SCHEME (coaching-tendency profiles with real W1