{"id": "corpus-intelligence/briefs/c01/reader-59/statking_backtesting.brief.md", "corpus": "corpus-intelligence", "kind": "brief", "chars": 2175, "equations": [], "text": "# statking-backtesting.md\n## What it is (1-2 sentences)\nA StatKing hardening-sprint artifact (generated by Codex on 2026-06-13) summarizing a brutal red-team audit of the StatKing NFL intelligence product, its seeded data foundation, and a handoff to Claude for premium UX work.\n## Key metrics/methods (formulas where given, else \"not specified\")\nnot specified. Audit severity ratings only (CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM) and seeded-inventory counts.\n## Data sources named\nNone named as live/active; the audit explicitly flags that legally usable data coverage is smaller than the seeded source universe, and that licensed route, pressure, coverage, tracking, PFF-like grades, and trenches data need contracts or first-party charting.\n## Findings (numbers and facts, not vibes)\n- CRITICAL finding: active, legally usable data coverage remains smaller than the seeded source universe.\n- HIGH: premium UX must explain trust, coverage, conflicts, and missing data \"in ten seconds.\"\n- HIGH: licensed route/pressure/coverage/tracking/PFF-like-grades/trenches data need contracts or first-party charting.\n- MEDIUM: backtesting and model proof are scaffolded with fixtures; they need historical production predictions.\n- Seeded foundation: 546 seeded sources, 800 candidate records, 500,000 candidate capacity, 2,200 discovery queries, 800 metric definitions.\n- Foundations listed: coverage, source trust, conflict, freshness, proof, comps, archetypes, alerts, versioning, competitive, king-standard.\n## Intelligence connections (tag each: QB-BEHAVIOR, COACHING, OL, TRUST-SIGNAL, SCHEME, OTHER)\n- OTHER: product/data-infrastructure audit; the flagged \"licensed route, pressure, coverage, trenches data need contracts or first-party charting\" is a data-acquisition signal relevant to OL (trenches/pressure) and QB-BEHAVIOR (coverage) lanes only as an INFERENCE about future data availability, not current content.\n## Engine-actionable? (yes/no + one-line what)\nNo — audit/inventory memo; the only actionable signal is the identified data gap (route, pressure, coverage, trenches need licensed feeds or first-party charting) which informs future acquisition priorities, not model wiring.\n"}
