{"id": "corpus-intelligence/briefs/c02/c02-r00/docs__ai__airwave__SIRIUSXM_CHANNEL_87_LISTENER_PROTOCOL.md.brief.md", "corpus": "corpus-intelligence", "kind": "brief", "chars": 4118, "equations": [], "text": "# docs/ai/airwave/SIRIUSXM_CHANNEL_87_LISTENER_PROTOCOL.md\n\n## What it is (1-2 sentences)\nThe intake protocol for SiriusXM Channel 87 (Fantasy Sports Radio) as Galaxy Sports Edge's primary satellite-radio intelligence source, built around founder-local-listening with a hard legal-acknowledgement gate — HELD until legal sign-off.\n\n## Key metrics/methods (formulas where given, else \"not specified\")\nnot specified — no formulas. Capture window: 05:00–23:00 CT (America/Chicago), 18 hours/day, enforced by `isWithinChannel87Window(hourCt)` in `channel-87-schedule.ts`. 12-column spreadsheet contract for manual notes: aired_at_ct | show | segment | speaker | paraphrased_claim | sport | entity | claim_type | confidence | rights_status | source_pointer | operator_status. Future worker design: 10-minute rolling audio segments → Whisper-class transcription → ClaimCandidate rows, segments deleted immediately.\n\n## Data sources named\nSiriusXM Channel 87 (Fantasy Sports Radio); founder's personally-owned SiriusXM subscription (founder-local-listening source policy, `operator_status = DRAFT`); manually imported CSV/TSV transcripts via `AIRWAVE_TRANSCRIPT_FILE_PATH`; env vars `AIRWAVE_ENABLED`, `AIRWAVE_SIRIUSXM_LEGAL_ACK`, `AIRWAVE_TRANSCRIPT_IMPORT_ENABLED`, `AIRWAVE_TRANSCRIPT_FILE_PATH`; readiness endpoint `/api/airwave/intake-readiness`; workers/airwave-listener/ (dry-run scaffolding); permanently excluded: `parker-stephens/siriusxm-activator`, `brendeni1/SiriusXM-Renewer`.\n\n## Findings (numbers and facts, not vibes)\n- Intake window: 05:00–23:00 CT, 18 hours/day; matches the core Airwave airing window in `pipeline.ts`; programming outside the window is not targeted. [OTHER]\n- Status HELD: CH87 intake, founder-local-listening and satellite-radio-context source policies are gated until `AIRWAVE_SIRIUSXM_LEGAL_ACK=true` (operator must review the SiriusXM Subscriber Agreement, confirm note-taking bounds, consult counsel, then set the env var). [TRUST-SIGNAL: rights-first gating]\n- Forbidden list (permanent): protected endpoint scraping, credential automation, DRM bypass, direct stream ripping, raw audio archives (no audio retained at any point), public verbatim transcripts (paraphrase only), automated recording of any kind, third-party activation tools. [TRUST-SIGNAL: hard no-list]\n- Safe first step today: manual note import (CSV/TSV, 12-column contract) with `rights_status` (owned/public/licensed) and `operator_status = draft`; no row reaches a public surface unless `operator_status = approved` AND `rights_status` is owned/public/licensed; review queue and source-policy gate are ready. [TRUST-SIGNAL]\n- Content focus of CH87: NFL/NBA/MLB injury reads and availability updates, DFS value commentary, waiver-wire guidance, betting-line context and market narratives, fantasy rankings/tier commentary, coaching and scheme notes. [COACHING: scheme notes; SCHEME: coaching/scheme content category]\n- Future local-listener worker (not yet implemented): 10-minute rolling segments → Whisper-class transcription (faster-whisper or whisper.cpp, MIT, on-device) → ClaimCandidate rows → review queue, never direct to public; candidate future adapters: Windows loopback audio capture, FFmpeg segment slicing. No commitment. [OTHER]\n\n## Intelligence connections (tag each: QB-BEHAVIOR, COACHING, OL, TRUST-SIGNAL, SCHEME, OTHER)\n- CH87's content focus explicitly includes injury/availability updates, DFS value, betting-line context, coaching and scheme notes — a named pipeline for scheme/coaching intelligence once the legal gate opens. [COACHING, SCHEME]\n- rights_status + operator_status two-gate review flow: a template for admitting any gray-rights football intelligence (pundit claims, radio reads) without laundering them into the engine. [TRUST-SIGNAL]\n- paraphrased_claim (never verbatim) + per-claim confidence: claim-shape discipline that maps directly onto the engine's signal-admission contracts. [OTHER]\n\n## Engine-actionable? (yes/no + one-line what)\nNo — the protocol is HELD behind legal ack; nothing flows to the engine until the founder sets the env gate, so no action until then.\n"}
{"id": "corpus-intelligence/briefs/c02/c02-r00/docs__ai__phase0__AI_CONTROL_PLANE_DESIGN_2026-07-22.md.brief.md", "corpus": "corpus-intelligence", "kind": "brief", "chars": 6317, "equations": ["amount WHERE id ="], "text": "# docs/ai/phase0/AI_CONTROL_PLANE_DESIGN_2026-07-22.md\n\n## What it is (1-2 sentences)\nThe 2026-07-22 Phase 2 implementation blueprint for the GSE AI control plane: five independent PRs (A task/policy contracts, B invocation ledger, C atomic budget reservations, D credit funding truth, E provider hardening) that make every LLM call policy-gated, cost-accounted, and fail-closed, superseding draft PRs #148/#151.\n\n## Key metrics/methods (formulas where given, else \"not specified\")\nCost-mode ordering for escalation control: NO_BILLABLE_EXTERNAL < CONFIRMED_CREDITS_ONLY < BUDGETED_CASH; effective mode = min(envMode, task.permittedModes) — a task may restrict below the environment, never escalate above it. Atomic reservation SQL: `UPDATE \"AiBudgetWindow\" SET \"reservedUsd\" = \"reservedUsd\" + $amount WHERE id = $window AND \"reservedUsd\" + \"settledUsd\" + $amount <= \"capUsd\" RETURNING id;` (zero rows → BudgetBlocked). Worst-case cost estimate = max output tokens × pricing version; missing pricing version fails closed for billable modes. Multi-scope reservations acquire windows in fixed lexicographic order inside one transaction (deadlock-free). Concurrency acceptance test: 100 parallel `executeAiTask` calls against a cap fitting 60 → exactly ≤ cap authorized, rest BudgetBlocked, `reservedUsd + settledUsd ≤ capUsd` holds under audit. Env-class resolution table: LLM_COST_MODE unset → production = ConfigurationError (deploy fails), preview/development/test = NO_BILLABLE_EXTERNAL; AI_ENV_CLASS unset derives from VERCEL_ENV/NODE_ENV and logs `envClassSource: 'explicit' | 'derived'`. EMERGENCY_RELIABILITY requires all three: LLM_COST_MODE=EMERGENCY_RELIABILITY + non-expired EMERGENCY_RELIABILITY_UNTIL ISO timestamp + EMERGENCY_REASON string, else ConfigurationError. Funding labels: pre-call CASH_EXPECTED | CREDIT_ELIGIBLE_UNCONFIRMED | CREDIT_EXPECTED_FROM_ACTIVE_GRANT | LOCAL_RESOURCE | EXTERNAL_FREE_ALLOWANCE_UNCONFIRMED | BLOCKED; post-billing reconciled CREDIT_APPLIED_CONFIRMED | CASH_CHARGED_CONFIRMED | NO_VENDOR_CHARGE_CONFIRMED | UNRECONCILED. Credit admission (CONFIRMED_CREDITS_ONLY): only with a fresh (observedAt within TTL), ACTIVATED/PARTIALLY_CONSUMED snapshot covering provider/account/region/model with remainingUsd ≥ worst-case estimate. Retry rules: AmbiguousCharge and ProviderRejected never auto-retried with same funds; PolicyBlocked/BudgetBlocked never retried.\n\n## Data sources named\nNOVA (owns credit-program lifecycle; #146's CreditProgramState is the seed; control plane consumes read-model snapshots, never writes). Phase 1A TrustedActor model; Phase 1E outbox pattern; model-router's surface union (`pick-explainer`, `journal-summary`, `model-court`, `calibration`); `provider-dispatch.ts`/`callClaude()` (apps/web/lib/claude-api/); import-boundary guard #158; credit-pool.ts (model-id mapping demoted to display hint `providerClassForModelId()`); model registry keyed by (family, version, provider, region); AWS credential chain (Bedrock), ADC/workload identity (Vertex).\n\n## Findings (numbers and facts, not vibes)\n- 5 PR sequence: A (contracts, zero runtime change) → B (ledger, additive) → C (reservations) → D (credit truth read-side) → E (hardening + call-site migration); each additive-Prisma-only, independently revertible; #148/#151 close with unit-by-unit preservation mapping when B lands. [OTHER]\n- Governing invariants: provider ≠ payer; cost mode explicit + fail-safe; no silent model substitution; telemetry failure never converts a successful paid call into a retry; one canonical entry point (`executeAiTask`); evidence before promotion. [TRUST-SIGNAL]\n- Ledger models: AiInvocation (statuses RUNNING | SUCCEEDED | FAILED | POLICY_BLOCKED | BUDGET_BLOCKED; telemetryStatus OK | DEGRADED separate), AiAttempt (statuses DISPATCHED | SUCCEEDED | FAILED | TIMEOUT | AMBIGUOUS; token counts incl. cacheRead/cacheWrite; @@unique([invocationId, ordinal])), AiFinancialAttribution (estimatedGrossUsd Decimal(12,6); creditGrantSnapshotId never inferred from model id — only from a grant snapshot). [OTHER]\n- The #151 defect fix: `providerUsed` written only after transport dispatch begins; every fallback creates a NEW AiAttempt row; a failed direct call is recorded as providerRequested='anthropic-direct', status='FAILED' — the ledger can never claim the failed provider \"served\" the request; \"cash billed\" never written by dispatch. [TRUST-SIGNAL: attribution-honesty rule]\n- Telemetry cannot break execution: non-throwing emitter; ledger failure sets telemetryStatus='DEGRADED' and enqueues to durable outbox; provider result returned regardless (test: kill the DB between provider success and ledger write → call still returns success). [OTHER]\n- Explicitly NOT in scope without owner decision: enabling BUDGETED_CASH anywhere; setting AI_ENV_CLASS=production values; activating EMERGENCY_RELIABILITY; any credit application or account mutation; deleting #148/#151 branches; forcing call-site migration in one sweep. [OTHER]\n- Typed error classes (11): Unauthenticated | Forbidden | InvalidInput | ConfigurationError | PolicyBlocked | BudgetBlocked | ProviderUnavailable | ProviderRejected | AmbiguousCharge | TelemetryDegraded | StoreUnavailable, each with `code` literal and `retriable: boolean`. [OTHER]\n\n## Intelligence connections (tag each: QB-BEHAVIOR, COACHING, OL, TRUST-SIGNAL, SCHEME, OTHER)\n- \"No silent model substitution\" / \"evidence before promotion\" invariants: the same anti-gaming discipline the engine needs for projection sources — a projection source may never be silently swapped; promotion requires test evidence. [TRUST-SIGNAL]\n- Attribution-honesty ledger (providerUsed only after dispatch; never claim a failed provider \"served\" a request): a pattern for engine signal attribution — never claim a signal drove a prediction it didn't touch. [TRUST-SIGNAL]\n- Fail-closed on missing pricing version (never guess a cost): parallels the engine's rule of never fabricating a metric when the source is missing. [TRUST-SIGNAL]\n- Remaining content is LLM-ops cost/governance machinery, not football intelligence. [OTHER]\n\n## Engine-actionable? (yes/no + one-line what)\nYes — adopt \"no silent projection-source substitution\" and \"attribution only for signals that actually fired\" as standing engine QA rules; everything else is platform ops.\n"}
